message: "If you use lines in research, cite it as below."
type: software
title: "lines: a merge-queue policy lab calibrated against production logs"
authors:
  - family-names: Pate
    given-names: Tyler
    alias: TGPSKI
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22637381
date-released: "2026-09-07"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22637380
    description: "Concept DOI, resolves to the latest release"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/TGPSKI/lines"
abstract: >-
  A fake GitLab API server and a policy simulator that drives merge-queue
  policies against it, including the unchanged production integration under a
  harness. Scenarios are derived from housekeeping logs and gated against a
  multidimensional calibration target before any policy comparison is read
  from them.
keywords:
  - merge queue
  - continuous integration
  - simulation
  - calibration
  - GitLab
  - qontract-reconcile
